section

open Set
open scoped Rockafellar

variable {𝕜 : Type*} [Field 𝕜] [LinearOrder 𝕜] [IsStrictOrderedRing 𝕜]
  [TopologicalSpace 𝕜] [OrderTopology 𝕜]
variable {E : Type*} [AddCommGroup E] [TopologicalSpace E] [Module 𝕜 E]
  [IsTopologicalAddGroup E] [ContinuousSMul 𝕜 E]

/-!
Source/core/bridge triage:

- `source-facing`: Theorem 18.7 says that a closed convex set containing no affine lines is the
  closure of the convex hull generated by its exposed points together with its exposed directions.
  `C.exposedDirections 𝕜`, `lineality[𝕜](C)`, `rayOfDirections`, written source-facingly as
  `ray`, and `mixedConvexHull`.
- `bridge/view`: the textbook affine-line exclusion is a companion bridge to
  `lineality[𝕜](C) = 0` on the nonempty branch, and the mixed generating set `S` containing
  both points and directions is rendered canonically as the mixed convex hull generated by the
  exposed points and the vectors lying on exposed direction rays, followed by topological closure.

Domain-style sampling used here:
- `Set.lineality_eq_zero_iff_not_hasAffineLine`;
- `eq_mixedConvexHull_extremePoints_rayOfExtremeDirections`;
- `extremePoints_subset_closure_exposedPoints`;
- `Set.exposedDirections`.

Primitive data vs derived API:
- primitive inputs: the closed convex set `C` together with the canonical owner-side condition
  `¬ HasAffineLine 𝕜 C`;
- derived API: the equality identifying `C` with the closure of the mixed convex hull generated by
  its exposed points and exposed directions;
- bridge/view: the lineality-owner wording `C = ∅ ∨ lineality[𝕜](C) = 0` is recovered by the
  companion theorem below.
- surface notation: the chapter notation `ray` keeps the ambient scalar `𝕜` inferable on the theorem
  surface, avoiding explicit parameter noise around `rayOfDirections`.
- ambient refinement: the surrounding owner theorems in this chapter already live on arbitrary
  finite-dimensional ordered topological vector spaces over `𝕜`, so the coordinate model
  `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)` is unnecessary here.

Layer target: `source-facing`, expressed directly through the chapter's existing exposed-point,
exposed-direction, and mixed-convex-hull owners.
-/

/-- Theorem 18.7, owner form: a closed convex set in a finite-dimensional ordered topological
vector space over `𝕜` containing no affine-line owner witness is the closure of the mixed convex
hull generated by its exposed points and its exposed directions. Specializing `𝕜 = ℝ`,
`E = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)` recovers the textbook `ℝ^n` formulation. -/
-- Proof sketch: Theorem 18.5 gives
-- `C = mixedConvexHull 𝕜 (C.extremePoints 𝕜)
--   (rayOfDirections (C.extremeDirections 𝕜))`. By
-- Theorem 18.6, every extreme point lies in the closure of `C.exposedPoints 𝕜`. A parallel
-- exposed-direction argument shows that every extreme direction lies in the closure generated by
-- `C.exposedDirections 𝕜`. Taking closures and using monotonicity of `mixedConvexHull` then
-- yields the required representation of `C`.
theorem eq_closure_mixedConvexHull_exposedPoints_rayOfExposedDirections
    {C : Set E} [FiniteDimensional 𝕜 (affineSpan 𝕜 C).direction]
    [FiniteDimensional 𝕜 (affineSpan 𝕜 (lin[𝕜](C))).direction]
    (hC_closed : IsClosed C) (hC_convex : Convex 𝕜 C)
    (hC_no_affineLine : ¬ HasAffineLine 𝕜 C) :
    C = closure (mconv[𝕜](C.exposedPoints 𝕜 | ray (C.exposedDirections 𝕜))) :=
  sorry

/-- Theorem 18.7, lineality-owner bridge: if `C` is empty or has vanishing lineality, then `C` is
the closure of the mixed convex hull generated by its exposed points and exposed directions. -/
theorem eq_closure_mixedConvexHull_exposedPoints_rayOfExposedDirections_of_empty_or_lineality_eq_zero
    {C : Set E} [FiniteDimensional 𝕜 (affineSpan 𝕜 C).direction]
    [FiniteDimensional 𝕜 (affineSpan 𝕜 (lin[𝕜](C))).direction]
    (hC_closed : IsClosed C) (hC_convex : Convex 𝕜 C)
    (hC_empty_or_lineality : C = ∅ ∨ lineality[𝕜](C) = 0) :
    C = closure (mconv[𝕜](C.exposedPoints 𝕜 | ray (C.exposedDirections 𝕜))) := by
  by_cases hC_empty : C = ∅
  · have hC_no_affineLine : ¬ HasAffineLine 𝕜 C := by
      simp [HasAffineLine, hC_empty]
    exact eq_closure_mixedConvexHull_exposedPoints_rayOfExposedDirections
      hC_closed hC_convex hC_no_affineLine
  · have hC_nonempty : C.Nonempty := Set.nonempty_iff_ne_empty.mpr hC_empty
    have hC_no_affineLine : ¬ HasAffineLine 𝕜 C := by
      rcases hC_empty_or_lineality with hC_empty' | hC_lineality
      · exact (hC_empty hC_empty').elim
      · exact (Set.lineality_eq_zero_iff_not_hasAffineLine hC_nonempty hC_closed hC_convex).1
          hC_lineality
    exact eq_closure_mixedConvexHull_exposedPoints_rayOfExposedDirections
      hC_closed hC_convex hC_no_affineLine

/-- Theorem 18.7, textbook bridge: a closed convex set containing no affine lines is the closure
of the mixed convex hull generated by its exposed points and its exposed directions. -/
theorem eq_closure_mixedConvexHull_exposedPoints_rayOfExposedDirections_of_no_affineLine
    {C : Set E} [FiniteDimensional 𝕜 (affineSpan 𝕜 C).direction]
    [FiniteDimensional 𝕜 (affineSpan 𝕜 (lin[𝕜](C))).direction]
    (hC_closed : IsClosed C) (hC_convex : Convex 𝕜 C)
    (hC_no_affineLine : ¬ ∃ x y : E, y ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ a : 𝕜, x + a • y ∈ C) :
    C = closure (mconv[𝕜](C.exposedPoints 𝕜 | ray (C.exposedDirections 𝕜))) := by
  simpa [HasAffineLine] using
    eq_closure_mixedConvexHull_exposedPoints_rayOfExposedDirections
      hC_closed hC_convex hC_no_affineLine

end
